1.9.2 Inheritance & Runtime Polymorphism

The exercise requires a genuine hierarchy, overridden methods, runtime dispatch, overloading, field hiding, static method hiding and debugging unexpected dispatch. 

Basic

53. What is inheritance?


54. What is runtime polymorphism?


55. What is method overriding?


56. What is dynamic method dispatch?


57. Create a parent/child hierarchy.


58. Override a method.


59. Invoke the method through a parent reference.



Intermediate

60. What is compile-time polymorphism?


61. What is method overloading?


62. Overloading vs overriding?


63. Demonstrate both in code.


64. What happens when the reference type differs from the object type?


65. Demonstrate field hiding.


66. Demonstrate static method hiding.



Advanced

67. Explain exactly why overridden methods are selected at runtime.


68. Explain why overloaded methods are selected at compile time.


69. Explain why fields are not dynamically dispatched like methods.


70. Explain static method hiding.


71. Trace a complex parent/child dispatch example.


72. Predict the output before execution.


73. Inspect the relevant bytecode.



Traps

74. Does a parent reference mean a parent object exists?


75. Are fields polymorphic?


76. Are static methods overridden?


77. Does overloading use runtime type?


78. Does overriding use compile-time type?


79. Does private method overriding exist?


80. Can constructors be overridden?



Design

81. Design:



PaymentProcessor
 ├── CardPayment
 ├── UpiPayment
 └── BankTransferPayment

82. Demonstrate runtime polymorphism.


83. Decide whether inheritance is appropriate.


84. Refactor a poor hierarchy into composition.



Debugging Challenges

85. Debug unexpected method dispatch.


86. Debug field hiding.


87. Debug static method hiding.


88. Debug an incorrect overload selection.


89. Predict the result before running.


90. Use runtime type information to explain the result.



Production

91. Design a pluggable payment system.


92. Decide interface vs abstract class vs composition.


93. Explain polymorphism's production benefits.


94. Explain potential allocation/performance implications.


95. Explain when inheritance should be avoided.



The source's performance exercises explicitly compare interface calls, virtual calls, final methods and static methods. 


