1.9.15 Pass-by-Value Debugging

The source explicitly requires four experiments: primitive reassignment, object mutation, reference reassignment, and mutation + reassignment. 

Basic

389. Is Java pass-by-value?


390. What is copied when a primitive is passed?


391. What is copied when an object reference is passed?



Intermediate

392. Predict Example A:



static void change(int value) {
    value = 100;
}

393. Predict Example B:



static void change(User user) {
    user.name = "Bob";
}

394. Predict Example C:



static void change(User user) {
    user = new User("Bob");
}

Advanced

395. Explain mutation vs reassignment.


396. Draw the reference/value model.


397. Explain why caller-visible mutation occurs.


398. Explain why caller reference reassignment doesn't occur.


399. Repeat the experiment with arrays.


400. Repeat with lists.


401. Repeat with maps.


402. Repeat with Strings.


403. Repeat with records.


404. Repeat with final references.



Traps

